lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109903","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109903.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109903.patch","merged_at":"2025-08-27T18:44:16Z"},"body":"Fixes #109171.\r\n\r\nIt is possible that the user changed an existing script to abstract after it was attached to a node. When this happens, the user needs to fix it, and we should keep track of the global class name to allow the \"Extend Script\" button to work.\r\n\r\nIn master: The \"Extend Script...\" button is hidden, and an unhelpful error message is printed. It is still possible for users to workaround the issue by \"Change Type...\" to a class extending the abstract class, or dragging a script into the inspector.\r\n\r\nIn this PR: The \"Extend Script...\" button appears, auto-fills with the class name, and a helpful error message is printed.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1220\" height=\"681\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-23 at 2 39 00 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e246355-e641-4c2f-8eee-6bf718ec04f1\" />\r\n\r\nThis PR still isn't perfect, for example we should have some way of marking the loaded scene as changed even though the user has made no changes, but I don't know if the PackedScene class has this capability. I'm open to suggestions.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://